# Production env for @forge/server. Copy to .env and fill in.
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=4000

# REQUIRED in production. Generate a strong value:
#   openssl rand -base64 48
JWT_SECRET=

# sqlite file — put it on a persistent disk/volume
FORGE_DB=/data/forge.db

# max upload size in bytes (default 50MB)
MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=52428800

# OPTIONAL: only when the web SPA is hosted separately from the API
# (e.g. SPA on Pinehoster + CDN, API on an external host). Build the web with:
#   VITE_API_BASE=https://api.factorialstudio.dev npm run build -w @forge/web
# Leave unset for the default single-origin deploy.
# VITE_API_BASE=

# ── Stripe billing (OPTIONAL) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave these unset to keep billing in dev mode (plans switch instantly, no card).
# When set, upgrades go through Stripe Checkout and plan changes are driven by the webhook.
#   1. Create two recurring Prices in the Stripe dashboard (Starter $49/mo, Studio $199/mo).
#   2. Add a webhook endpoint → https://app.factorialstudio.dev/api/billing/webhook
#      subscribed to ALL of: checkout.session.completed, customer.subscription.created,
#      customer.subscription.updated, customer.subscription.deleted. (created is required —
#      a new Checkout subscription fires it, and that's what sets the plan.)
#      Copy its signing secret into STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_STARTER=price_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_STUDIO=price_...
# Absolute SPA base URL for Checkout return links (used only if the request Origin is missing):
# PUBLIC_URL=https://app.factorialstudio.dev

# ── Transactional email (OPTIONAL) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Used for email verification and password-reset links. Without RESEND_API_KEY the server
# keeps messages in an in-memory dev outbox (and logs them) — fine locally, but in production
# NOTHING is delivered, so set these before launch.
#   1. Create a Resend account (resend.com), verify your sending domain (e.g. factorialstudio.dev).
#   2. Create an API key and set MAIL_FROM to a verified address.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# MAIL_FROM="Factorial AdLab <noreply@factorialstudio.dev>"

# ── Support / ops (OPTIONAL) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ticket, bug-report and contact-form notifications go here (default contact@factorialstudio.com):
# SUPPORT_EMAIL=contact@factorialstudio.com
# Platform admins (comma-separated). Listed addresses become admins at their next sign-in and get the
# Admin console (users, support inbox, bugs, contact, jobs, reminders). Admins can promote others.
# ADMIN_EMAILS=qasim@factorialstudio.com
# Send reminder emails automatically once a day (never-exported after 3 days; dormant after 14 days).
# Off by default — admins can run / dry-run them from the console.
# REMINDERS_AUTO=1

# ── Unity plugin distribution (OPTIONAL) ────────────────────────────────────
# Signs each plugin download's licence. When unset, a 2048-bit RSA key is generated once and kept in the
# database (fine on Render's persistent disk). Set it only to pin the key across databases (PKCS#8 PEM;
# "\n" escapes are accepted on one line).
# PLUGIN_SIGNING_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----"
# Refuse plugin requests older than this version with an "update the plugin" message:
# PLUGIN_MIN_VERSION=0.2.0
# Refuse plugin copies without a licence (i.e. installed from source rather than downloaded):
# PLUGIN_REQUIRE_LICENSE=1

# ── Cloudflare Turnstile bot check (OPTIONAL) ───────────────────────────────
# Protects sign-up, forgot-password and the contact form. Off unless BOTH are set. Create a widget in
# Cloudflare (Turnstile → Add widget, hostname app.factorialstudio.dev) and paste its keys. The site key is
# public (served to the browser); the secret stays on the server. For local testing Cloudflare's dummy
# keys always pass: site 1x00000000000000000000AA, secret 1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA.
# TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
